{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "The History of PHP"}, {"type": "position", "content": 12}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 2}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "You can use these words to talk about the history of PHP."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Understand information about web applications, their principles and basic concepts in a range of  work contexts.   Describe applications for an operating system for personal computers in a range of  work contexts. "}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Reads and Writes effective texts in English showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context. \t  Exchanges simple information on web applications, and applications for operating systems for personal computers."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe7n6le02ob12re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "trace back "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to follow something to its origins"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(phrasal verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: But that's not the reality; we can trace back the origin of PHP to 1994."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n6le02ob12aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "tremendous "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "remarkable, very noticeable"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: they created PHP 3.0, it was strong, it had a tremendous success, it was a object-oriented programming language"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n6le02ob12aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "bug "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a fail in a software"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Rasmus released the source code so people could use it as they pleased, they even pointed out the bugs it had."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n6le02ob12aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "unsolved "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "referring to no answer; mistery "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: the main problem was still unresolved, there were many contributions, but the only person in charge of developing it was Ramus."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n6le02ob12aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "surge "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to appear and grow"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The eCommerce was surging and it needed a stronger PHP."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n6le02ob12aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Look for information about the PHP usages in software development companies."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write down some notes and design a chart where you show the advantages and disadvantages of it."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share with your partner and check any new fact about PHP."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I look for information about PHP usages. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I create chart to show advantages and disadvantages of it."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I talk about PHP implementation in software companies. "}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Phrasal Verbs"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<b>Phrasal verbs</b> are verbs made up of two words ( a verb + a preposition/adverb). They have a different meaning than usual."}, {"type": "text", "content": "There are many phrasal verbs, but in this lesson, we will focus on three.</br></br>  <strong>Write down:</strong> To take notes of something and write them in notebook or similar.</br> <strong>Write off:</strong> To predict that something will end badly.</br> <strong>Point out:</strong> To signal or show something.</br> <strong>Make up:</strong> To create or design.</br></br> Examples:</br><i> You should <b>write down </b>what I'll explain today, it will appear on the next exam.</br> Mike's teacher has <b>written </b>him <b>off</b> as a failure in class, he never handed in the project.</br> To answer this question, I need to <b>point out</b> different possible answers.</br> The guys that <b>made up</b> Tumbler are very famous now.</i></br>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Rasmus Lerdorf is PHP creator, back in 1994, he made it up with the original purpose of tracking visits on his online resume."}, {"type": "example", "content": "In 1995, Rasmus released the source code so people could use it as they pleased, they even pointed out the bugs it had. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "It was similar to Perl, but it wasn't as powerful, it was simple, limited and inconsistent, people liked it, but they were writing it off. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Did you write down all of that?  I might ask this in the next class."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Writing a Descriptive Paragraph"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<b>Descriptive paragraphs </b>permit you to engage your readers with your text thanks to the way you give detailed information about a topic "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You usually write a <b>descriptive paragraph </b>when you want to illustrate events, places or people in detail.<br><br>You can follow these tips when writing a descriptive paragraph. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<b>First, choose the topic that you want to talk about. </b><br> It's crucial for you to look for an interesting topic with different characteristics that you can describe."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<b>Second, look for detailed information about your topic. </b><br> Before writing any text, you have to read, research and acquaint yourself with this topic. So, you can give more information about. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<b>Third, introduce your topic. </b><br> You can start your opening lines with general, but relevant and striking information about the person, place or event you want to describe. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<b>Forth, get your readers' attention. </b><br> Be as descriptive as possible, using strong adjectives. In this way, you can appeal your readers' senses. Plus, you can describe smells, textures, tastes, etc. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<b>Fifth, support your ideas. </b><br> Write two supporting ideas in which you express how the events feel, and use emotions and feelings to finish your text."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<b>Finally, write correctly. </b><br> Throughout your text, remember to connect your ideas with linking words (In addition, Moreover, Furthermore, Plus\u2026). It permits that your text can be enjoyable to read. "}], "type": "learning_points"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"video_src": "enpe7n6le02ob12re5vsc01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "", "id": 0, "text": ""}]}, "type": "video"}], "type": "video", "_data": [], "id": 5, "title": ""}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"time": "100", "image": "enpe7n6le02ob12re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "You might think PHP is very modern and contemporary, but it's not. We can trace back the origin of PHP to 1994.\nRasmus Lerdorf was the PHP creator in 1994. He made it up with the original purpose of tracking visits on his online resume. The full name of it was \u201cPersonal Home Page Tools\u201d, but people said PHP tools. It was a simple set of common gateway interface, and it was written in a programming language.\nRasmus rewrote it to include more functions; plus, in 1995, Rasmus released the source code, so people could use it as they pleased. Indeed, they pointed out the bugs it had."}, {"time": "50500", "image": "enpe7n6le02ob12re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "Rasmus changed the name to Forms Interpreter or FI, it was similar to Perl, but it wasn't as powerful. It was simple, limited and inconsistent, people liked it, but they were writing it off.\nIn April 1996, Rasmus changed the name again, it was PHP/FI. Constantly, improvements were done; then it was named PHP 2.0 which was very famous for two years. Nevertheless, the main problem was still unresolved, and there were many contributions, but the only person in charge of developing it was Rasmus.\nThe eCommerce was surging, and it needed a stronger PHP. Two men, Andi Gutmans and Zeev Suraski joined Rasmus in his efforts, they created PHP 3.0, it was strong, it had a tremendous success, it was an object-oriented programming language. They kept working, and it 1998, they released PHP 4.0 more powerful than before."}, {"time": "122000", "image": "enpe7n6le02ob12re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "Finally, what we use today is PHP 5.0, released in 2004. It has more features, and we might consider that million of domains around the world are using it. Did you write down all of that? I might ask this in the next class."}], "coverimg": "enpe7n6le02ob12re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "enpe7n6le02ob12re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 6, "title": ""}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can understand written information about the history of PHP. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can use t